			],
			"Message": "build(deps): bump pnpm/action-setup from 6.0.1 to 6.0.3\n\nBumps [pnpm/action-setup](https://github.com/pnpm/action-setup) from 6.0.1 to 6.0.3.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/pnpm/action-setup/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/pnpm/action-setup/compare/v6.0.1...v6.0.3)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: pnpm/action-setup\n  dependency-version: 6.0.3\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>",
			"SHA": "4cb9b84a242e91fbeb53db024b850219900ae8b7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-21T21:45:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				80,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Use static fs imports in StripDanglingSourceMaps\n\nReplace dynamic `await import(\"node:fs/promises\")` calls with the top-of-file static bindings in the StripDanglingSourceMaps function. Dynamic imports crash with \"Vite module runner has been closed\" because this runs inside `astro:build:done`, after Vite tears down its ModuleRunner.\n\nAlso switch to `readdir` with `{ withFileTypes: true }` to get `Dirent[]` instead of `string[]`, enabling type-safe `Entry.name` and `Entry.isDirectory()` checks instead of separate `stat` calls.\n\nThese changes ensure the source map stripping process (Step 11b in CopyVSCode) runs reliably during the build.",
			"SHA": "42372a213a22f0c6551f2cf293289b60feddc024"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-21T20:58:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				80,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add vscode-file and vscode-webview-resource to CSP\n\nAdd two new URI schemes (`vscode-file:` and `vscode-webview-resource:`) to the Content Security Policy across all editor entry points (Browser, BrowserProxy, Electron, Mountain, index). These schemes are required to load resources from the VS Code platform code that gets copied during the build.\n\nAdditionally, implement Step 11b in the CopyVSCode build process to strip dangling `//# sourceMappingURL=…` comments from copied JS files that don't have a sibling .map file. Without this, Safari fetches the missing maps, receives 404 HTML, and surfaces a SyntaxError for every such file on every page load.",
			"SHA": "351cc1bcbe5552b96f844736da36fe2e65fce75b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-21T18:32:33Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				80,
				8
			],
			"Message": "chore(Sky): Update product metadata and standardize em-dash formatting\n\n- Bump version from 0.1.0 to 1.118.0 in product.json\n- Update quality from 'stable' to 'development'\n- Change nameLong to 'Land Editor' and commit to 'dev'\n- Add embedderIdentifier field for desktop builds\n- Replace em-dashes (—) with hyphens (-) in comments and documentation across CHANGELOG.md, DeepDive.md, OTELBridge.ts, PostHogBridge.ts, Mountain.astro, TelemetryBridge.astro, and astro.config.ts\n\nThe version bump to 1.118.0 reflects the continued development progress on the Sky UI component layer, with updated product metadata for the next development cycle.",
			"SHA": "f53785d4449f68ab86bfc65f15efd612a0e73d99"
		},
